[E0313] Error: an arm that takes `label` cannot have a guard
    ╭─[ err/550_var_name_before_a_guard/main.wip:13:28 ]
    │
 13 │         .Named(var label, ..) if label.len() > 2 => label.push("angle")
    │         ──────────┬──────────    ───────┬───────
    │                   ╰─────────────────────────────── `label` is `String`, which owns memory
    │                                         │
    │                                         ╰───────── a guard
    │
    │ Help: bind it without `var`, and take what the arm needs in its body
    │
    │ Note: a guard runs once the pattern has taken the value apart, so a guard that fails would leave it half taken
────╯
